In the game, food you cook keeps part of the Blight contamination of its raw meat or water. So your Blight keeps rising even when you eat only cooked food, and you end up drinking Spotted Red Mushroom Soup again and again to bring it down, at a cost to your health. Food also spoils fast. With this mod, the fire makes food safe, and your stores last. The blight zones and the other Blight risks stay as in the game.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Clean cooking and smoking.[/b] Food from a fire or a Smoke Rack starts with no contamination, even from contaminated meat or water. This includes boiled water, teas, soups, and jerky. Food can still pick up contamination later, for example next to Blighted Fungus.[/*]
[*][b]Slower spoilage.[/b] Food, raw meat, hides, and other animal products spoil 5 times more slowly, wherever they are. Carcasses stay in the world 5 times as long, and the meat in them spoils 5 times more slowly too.[/*]
[*][b]Better preserving.[/b] A Covered Clay Jar or a Covered Glass Bottle slows spoilage twice as much, now also in your backpack. Salt preserves food twice as fast, and berry juice turns into vinegar twice as fast.[/*]
[*][b]Spoils in.[/b] The tooltip of each item that spoils shows the time left, such as "Spoils in 1 day 6 hours".[/*]
[*][b]Fair play.[/b] Raw food, Blight sources such as Blighted Fungus, and the blight zones stay as in the game.[/*]
[*][b]Save safety.[/b] The mod writes nothing to your save, so you can remove it at any time. Made for single player: co-op is not tested.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Spoil times[/b][/size]
[table]
[tr][th]Item[/th][th]Game[/th][th]5x[/th][th]10x[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Raw Deer Meat[/td][td]8 hours[/td][td]1.6 days[/td][td]3.2 days[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Cooked Wolf Meat[/td][td]19 hours[/td][td]3.9 days[/td][td]7.7 days[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Piece of Jerky[/td][td]7.7 days[/td][td]39 days[/td][td]77 days[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Mushrooms[/td][td]35 hours[/td][td]7.2 days[/td][td]14.5 days[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Deer Hide[/td][td]40 hours[/td][td]8.3 days[/td][td]16.5 days[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Carcass in the world[/td][td]28 hours[/td][td]5.8 days[/td][td]11.6 days[/td][/tr]
[/table]

Below 5 °C, the cold slows spoilage further, in the game and with the mod. The mod uses 5x by default, and you can set the slowdown for food and for animal products separately, from 1 (as in the game) to 20, or 0 for no spoilage (see Configuration).

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The Last Plague: Blight 0.12.7 or later.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/9]BepInEx for The Last Plague: Blight[/url].[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/9]BepInEx[/url].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Plague\BepInEx\plugins\StayFresh.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]StayFresh.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
To change mod settings, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.thelastplagueblight.stayfresh.cfg[/font] while the game is closed (see [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-stay-fresh/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for every setting). Changes apply at the next game start.

